From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:51:04 +0000
Subject: Check for updates in the hawkff/cromite releases

The update check sent a HEAD request for the arm64_ChromePublic.apk file of
the latest uazo/cromite release, read the version from the redirect, and
offered that file in the menu when it was newer. Those builds have another
package name and signing key, so they cannot update this browser: installing
one adds a second browser next to it. The check and the download now use the
latest hawkff/cromite release, with the same file names.

When no release is found, the check is meant to wait one hour before it tries
again, but the stored time made it due at once, so the request was sent again
each time the browser returned to the foreground. It now waits one hour. The
check still runs only when "Allow checking for updates" is on in About.

